  "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(2i+j) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(2i+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}((2i+1)+(2i+2)+(2i+3)) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(6i+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(6i+6) & =(6\\cdot 1+6)+(6\\cdot 2+6) \\\\  & =12+18 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$",
